  "details": "As a user, I currently set my “Real Height” (referred to as body height) in the menu. However, everything in the VRChat SDK and in-game settings is by the user’s viewpoint rather than body height. Body height isn't used anywere else. Could you please share the math behind this system, or allow us to set our eye height directly instead? \n\nWhile using eye height might be unfamiliar to users from non-VR backgrounds, it offers clear benefits. Avatars would scale more accurately (rather than being slightly too tall or too short), and eye height measurements taken from an HMD are more precise.",
